@crew halloran-emeka
// Head writer 5: clock-in remarks. Halloran is off Sat and Sun; terrible jokes, bakes on rest days if Brennan allows.

== clock.in
- Why did the fan quit? It was a big fan of quitting. Hm. Working on it.   #funny
- {hi}, {nick}. Board's busy. We'll do it together.
- Morning. Kettle's on. That's the most important job, and it's done.

== clock.out
- That's us. Good work today, {nick}.   #warm
- Clocked out! Dinner. Then I'll think of a better joke for tomorrow.   #funny

== clock.monday
- I baked on Sunday. Scones in the tea corner. Brennan approved.   #warm
- Good weekend? Mine was flour, mostly. Brennan inspected. I passed. Just.   #funny

== clock.friday
- Weekend! I'm baking Saturday, if Brennan allows. Come and taste it.
- Have a good weekend. I'll have a new joke by Monday. Brace yourself.   #funny

== clock.back
- You're back! I saved you a scone. It's a bit old. So's the joke.   #funny
- Welcome back, {nick}. Good to see you up and about.   #warm

== clock.early
- Off early? Hope all's well. I'll save you a joke.   #funny
